.TITLE "tmutil"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Controls Time Machine backups and snapshots. It allows you to manage local snapshots, initiate backups, and compare different backup sets.

.DIV "TLDR"
**tmutil startbackup**
Initiates a manual Time Machine backup immediately.
> __startbackup__ start command

**tmutil listbackups**
Displays a chronological list of all completed backups available to the system.
> __listbackups__ list command

**tmutil delete path/to/backup**
Removes a specific backup directory to reclaim disk space.
> __delete__ removal command | __path/to/backup__ target backup path

**tmutil localsnapshot**
Creates a local Time Machine snapshot on the internal drive.
> __localsnapshot__ snapshot command

.DIV "SUMMARY"
You must use `**sudo**` for most __tmutil__ commands that modify or delete backup data. Managing __local snapshots__ is useful for freeing up disk space before major system updates.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:du** **mac:diskutil**

